#  neural network classifies an image into four categories. The actual class distribution is 
Y=[0,1,0,0], and the predicted probability distribution is P=[0.1,0.6,0.2,0.1]. The developer 
wants to evaluate the prediction error and compare the predicted distribution with the actual 
distribution. 
Write a Python program to calculate the cross-entropy loss and KL divergence between the 
actual and predicted distributions, and to visualize the two distributions.




import numpy as np

Y = np.array([0,1,0,0])
P = np.array([0.1,0.6,0.2,0.1])

CE = -np.sum(Y*np.log(P))
KL = np.sum(Y[Y>0]*np.log(Y[Y>0]/P[Y>0]))
print("Cross entropy:", CE)
print("KL divergence:", KL)
